Drives its own private GC state (its own `gcBindMemory`/`gcInit`-bound arena) and
every assertion is about that private heap: how many bytes of spans it mapped for
a burst, how many it gave back once the burst became garbage, and whether it
still serves the same size class afterwards. None of them depends on whether the
ambient (libbitrt) collector ever runs — the objects it allocates are the private
collector's and are invisible to the ambient one, and the collections that matter
are the explicit `gcCollectRoots` calls this program makes itself.
